  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The angle of deviation through a prism is minimum when&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/cbc0fa84-a47d-40f7-beb8-f02a05981a07-image.png\" style=\"width: 291px; height: 164px;\" /></p><p>(A) Incident ray and emergent ray are symmetric to the prism</p><p>(B) The refracted ray inside the prism becomes parallel to its base</p><p>(C) Angle of incidence is equal to that of the angle of emergence</p><p>(D) When angle of emergence is double the angle of incidence</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jvIXs",
      "text": "Statements (A),(B)&nbsp;and (C)&nbsp;are true",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NslS8",
      "text": "Only statement (D) is true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "abl7d",
      "text": "Only statements (A) and (B) are true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4M184",
      "text": "Statements (B) and (C) are true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As per the figure given in question, we are considering it an Isosceles Prism.</p><p>Deviation is minimum in a prism when :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and ray <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is parallel to base of prism.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/0689da10-ae62-488b-971d-c926af24c50d-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 160px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
